recommend keep-going A Rye-native Ed25519 keypair-and-signature now stands whole beside the verifier — the Lotus signed carry, Kumara identity, Vault, and Comlink can both sign and verify with no std.crypto or C library, the maintainer's own key awaiting only its gate. Non-gated cruxes still open on the same GREEN base field: X25519 key agreement (the Diffie-Hellman side of Kumara, over the montgomery ladder), and Monocypher-source parity once the held vendor fetch clears. The Lotus signed-carry composition — wrapping sign/verify into the "who made this record" wire shape (crypto over the ALES cable frame) — is now buildable and durable. Next durable rung: whichever of those.
